\nYiddish\nYoruba\nZulu\n1\nPrev Next\nAuditor/Treasurer\nSub Menu\nRelated Pages\nDepartment Information\nAuditor/Treasurer Services\nAuditor FAQs\nContacts for Officials\nElections\nElections Home\nBecome an Election Judge\nCampaign Finance Reports\nHow to File as a Candidate\nHow to Vote or Return a Ballot\nPast Election Results & Information\nPolling Places\nReturn To Auditor/Treasurer Page\nFee Schedule\nHemp & Cannabis\nLicenses & Permits\nMobile/Manufactured Homes\nNotary Commission Filing\nPassports\nProperty Tax Refunds\nProperty Tax Search & Information\nOnline Property Tax Payments\nResources\nTax Forfeited Land Sales\nVital Statistics\nUpcoming Events/Meetings\nFull calendar\nHome\nDepartments\nAuditor/Treasurer\nMonday - Friday 8am - 4:30pm\n507-765-3811 & 507-765-4701\nauditor@fillmorecountymn.gov\nfax: 507-765-2803 |\n|\nHeather Broadwater\n101 Fillmore Street PO Box 627\nPreston, MN 55965\n|\n***Emails have changed!! Please reach out to our office using one of the following emails as of 8-18-2026.***\nauditor@fillmorecountymn.gov - Reach the entire Auditor/Treasurer staff\nelections@fillmorecountymn.gov - Reach the entire Elections staff\nThe Auditor/Treasurer is an appointed position made by Fillmore County. Basic duties of the Fillmore County Auditor/Treasurer's Office include:\nCalculate tax rates and taxes due based on the levy request submitted by the county, cities, school districts, and special taxing districts\nPrepare Truth in Taxation Notices and Property Tax Statements for every taxable real and personal property in the county\nMaintain and collect property taxes and distribute the tax collections to the proper taxing district\nWork with tax credits and special tax deferments\nAdminister Tax Increment Financing as it pertains to tax calculation\nMaintain special assessments for cities and townships, apply the payments for collection and remit the annual installments to the proper taxing district\nConduct Tax Forfeiture Land Sales on behalf of the county\nMaintain the tax roll through updates to ownership, splits, combinations, and transfers\nChief Elections Administrator for the county\nProcess liquor, gambling, auctioneer, tobacco, and sale of cannabinoid licenses\nResponsible for Fillmore County Vital Statistics which provides records of marriage certificates and registration of ordination\nRegistration of Notary Commissions for the State of Minnesota\nResponsible for passport administration\nThe Auditor/Treasurer's Office is required by law to maintain records for all funds received and expended.\nOffice Hours:\nMonday - Friday\n8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\n(open through noon hour)\nTo view map or obtain directions, click link below:\nView Larger Map\nProperty Tax Search\nProperty Tax Search & Statements (Beacon)\nShare this page\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.co.fillmore.mn.us/departments/auditor_treasurer/index.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\nEmployee Resources\nCounty Email\nIntranet\nTimekeeping System\nVPN\nContact\n101 Fillmore Street\nPreston, MN 55965\nDirectory\nAbout Us\nFillmore County is located on the southern border of Minnesota. Named for Millard Fillmore, the 13th President of the United States, our community is both agricultural and historic.\nFillmore County Mission Statement: Fillmore County's mission is to provide quality services to its citizens in an efficient, cost-effective manner.\n© 2026 Fillmore CO | Powered by revize , The Government Website Experts |\nLogin\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nundefined\nundefined\nundefined",
